  "provenance": [
    "Native flows use debug smoke builds. Reflow, PDF and mixed-size PDF navigation flows were rerun for the timing corrections; the unchanged notebook and AT-SPI flows retain their previous passing runs. The subsequent storage-permission fix reran both full Rust suites and strict Clippy, with focused filesystem checks; native behavior did not change.",
    "The first reflow run exposed a test setup issue: selecting source text can replace the GTK editor primary selection on X11. The regression compares notebook state immediately before and after capture. All final checks pass.",
    "Earlier September evidence remains historical; this record does not assert those measurements were rerun.",
    "The first timing run passed all application assertions but its restart harness timed out because concurrent Cargo tests replaced the smoke executable with a normal build. All three focused wrappers were rerun successfully using a fixed copy of the smoke binary; these final results include restart checks."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "The Docker host prohibits unprivileged user namespaces. Native tests set WEBKIT_DISABLE_SANDBOX_THIS_IS_DANGEROUS=1 inside this disposable isolated container; these runs do not qualify the WebKit sandbox. No application sandbox setting changed.",
    "AT-SPI assertions are tree/action checks, not a human Orca usability session.",
    "No system installation, actual user-session actions, Wayland scale/performance requalification, or full MVP release qualification was performed. The documented ordinary-reading, human accessibility, and performance gates remain open."
  ],
  "pdf_keyboard_followup": {
    "finding": "SOL-F1: Papers keyboard scroll actions bypassed wheel and selection-changed invalidation.",
    "regression": "Five intended assertions failed before connecting the native scroll action; all 62 PDF passage assertions pass after the fix. The fixture movement check accepts movement within a tall page as well as page-number changes.",
    "assertions_added": 8,
    "behavior": "Keyboard navigation clears the source selection token, Save availability, temporary quotation highlight, and pending passage navigation while programmatic passage restoration keeps its highlight."
  },
  "hosted_review_followup": {
    "documentation": "The original F01/F02 description is explicitly historical, and F02a is marked delivered.",
    "selection": "Focused-chapter deselection and whitespace invalidate capture and temporary marks; delayed deselection from an inactive chapter preserves a newer capture or highlight. Six WebKit adapter assertions cover these cases and the fallback-selection exemption.",
    "pdf_quotation": "Full saved quotations must consist of the ordered per-page fragment text plus whitespace separators. A Rust regression covers Unicode, repeated fragments, normal separators, mismatches, reordering, uncovered text and overlap."
  },
  "hosted_review_timing_followup": {
    "reflow_cancellation": "Recovery snapshots request and selection generations and aborts after document loading and each scan yield. New navigation and appearance commands invalidate selection before queueing. Four WebKit regressions cover navigation, superseding requests, valid replacement requests and delayed document loading.",
    "pdf_page_snapshot": "Paged PDF changes retain the announced page synchronously while deferring coordinates. Stale allocation samples cannot overwrite that page. Four native regressions cover immediate save/bookmark/settings and deferred sampling; 85 mixed-size PDF/navigation assertions also pass."
